<p class="hint tool-disc">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They are not a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>How depreciation is estimated</h2>
<p>The calculator uses straight-line depreciation, which is age divided by expected life, capped at the maximum you choose. Real estimates may use condition adjustments, different life tables or non-depreciable items such as permits and debris removal, so treat the result as a planning figure.</p>
<h2>Typical life expectancies in estimates</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Common range</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th>Asphalt architectural shingles</th><td>25–30 years</td></tr><tr><th>Slate roof</th><td>60–100+ years</td></tr><tr><th>Cedar shingle roof</th><td>20–30 years</td></tr><tr><th>Interior paint</th><td>8–12 years</td></tr><tr><th>Carpet</th><td>8–12 years</td></tr><tr><th>Hardwood flooring</th><td>Long life; refinishing 15–25 years</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2>Getting the holdback released</h2>
<p>Most policies release recoverable depreciation once repairs are completed within a set time. Send final invoices and photos of the finished work. The <a href="/ct-claim-tools/claim-calendar-builder/">claim calendar builder</a> can remind you before that window closes.</p>

<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Should labor be depreciated?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Treatment of labor depreciation varies by policy, state and court decisions. Ask your carrier to explain its approach in writing and compare it with your policy.</p></div></details><details><summary>What happens if I don’t repair?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Under most replacement cost policies you keep the ACV payment but may not recover the held-back depreciation.</p></div></details></div>
